remarks.para:
When  is true, the compiler (via nullable reference types and
) knows this value is not null, enabling safe access
without null checks.

example.code:
Response<int> Calculate() => new(true, 42);

int result = Calculate(); // Implicitly extracts the 42
Console.WriteLine(result); // 42

